    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.diff\n\n### Question\n\nI was wondering how to setup mini.diff keymap to reset the hunk under my cursors.\r\n\r\nAny attempt i have resets the hunk at the current line (not the entire hunk) or resets all hunks in buffer. Similar to how [gitsigns](https://github.com/lewis6991/gitsigns.nvim/blob/main/README.md?plain=1#L41) works with hunks ",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.diff</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I was wondering how to setup mini.diff keymap to reset the hunk under my cursors.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Any attempt i have resets the hunk at the current line (not the entire hunk) or resets all hunks in buffer. Similar to how <a href=\"https://github.com/lewis6991/gitsigns.nvim/blob/main/README.md?plain=1#L41\">gitsigns</a> works with hunks</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.diff\nQuestion\nI was wondering how to setup mini.diff keymap to reset the hunk under my cursors.\nAny attempt i have resets the hunk at the current line (not the entire hunk) or resets all hunks in buffer. Similar to how gitsigns works with hunks",
