            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "'mini.diff' defines a set of [mappings](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-diff.html#minidiff.config-mappings). Among them are:\r\n\r\n- \"`mappings.reset` keys can be used to reset hunks inside visual/operator region.\". By default it is `gH`.\r\n- \"`mappings.textobject` keys define 'hunk range under cursor' textobject which can be used in Operator-pending mode as target for operator (like [d](https://neovim.io/doc/user/helptag.html?tag=d), [y](https://neovim.io/doc/user/helptag.html?tag=y), apply/reset hunks, etc.).\". By default it is `gh`.\r\n\r\nSo to reset hunk under cursor with default mappings, type `gHgh` (apply reset operator for `gh` textobject). Tip: it is dot-repeatable; meaning you can type `gHgh`, navigate to the next hunk with `]h`, and press `.` to reset it.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">'mini.diff' defines a set of <a href=\"https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-diff.html#minidiff.config-mappings\" rel=\"nofollow\">mappings</a>. Among them are:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>\"<code class=\"notranslate\">mappings.reset</code> keys can be used to reset hunks inside visual/operator region.\". By default it is <code class=\"notranslate\">gH</code>.</li>\n<li>\"<code class=\"notranslate\">mappings.textobject</code> keys define 'hunk range under cursor' textobject which can be used in Operator-pending mode as target for operator (like <a href=\"https://neovim.io/doc/user/helptag.html?tag=d\" rel=\"nofollow\">d</a>, <a href=\"https://neovim.io/doc/user/helptag.html?tag=y\" rel=\"nofollow\">y</a>, apply/reset hunks, etc.).\". By default it is <code class=\"notranslate\">gh</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">So to reset hunk under cursor with default mappings, type <code class=\"notranslate\">gHgh</code> (apply reset operator for <code class=\"notranslate\">gh</code> textobject). Tip: it is dot-repeatable; meaning you can type <code class=\"notranslate\">gHgh</code>, navigate to the next hunk with <code class=\"notranslate\">]h</code>, and press <code class=\"notranslate\">.</code> to reset it.</p>",
            "bodyText": "'mini.diff' defines a set of mappings. Among them are:\n\n\"mappings.reset keys can be used to reset hunks inside visual/operator region.\". By default it is gH.\n\"mappings.textobject keys define 'hunk range under cursor' textobject which can be used in Operator-pending mode as target for operator (like d, y, apply/reset hunks, etc.).\". By default it is gh.\n\nSo to reset hunk under cursor with default mappings, type gHgh (apply reset operator for gh textobject). Tip: it is dot-repeatable; meaning you can type gHgh, navigate to the next hunk with ]h, and press . to reset it.",
